  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Terbinafine is an antifungal medicine used to treat fungal skin and nail infections such as ringworm, athlete's foot, and nail fungus. It is widely used, both as a topical and an oral treatment, and is included on the WHO list of essential medicines.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q415259&quot;>Wikidata Q415259</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>terbinafine</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>D01AE15, D01BA02</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB00857&quot;>DB00857</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/1549008&quot;>1549008</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:9448&quot;>9448</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q415259&quot;>Q415259</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C21H25N</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>291.438 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
